ume>29</volume>:<fpage>961</fpage>&#x02013;985.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16026885</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Laurido, C., S. Candia, D. Wolff, and R. Latorre. <year>1991</year>. Proton modulation of a Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-activated K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel from rat skeletal muscle incorporated into planar bilayers. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>1025</fpage>&#x02013;1042.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1662682</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Laver, D.R. <year>1992</year>. Divalent cation block and competition between divalent and monovalent cations in the large-conductance K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel from <italic>Chara australis.</italic> <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>269</fpage>&#x02013;300.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1402783</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, Y., M. Holmgren, M.E. Jurman, and G. Yellen. <year>1997</year>. Gated access to the pore of a voltage-dependent K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>175</fpage>&#x02013;184.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9247273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, Y., S.P. Sompornpisut, and E. Perozo. <year>2001</year>. Structure of the KcsA channel intracellular gate in the open state. <source>Nat. Struct. Biol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>883</fpage>&#x02013;887.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11573095</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Lu, Z., and R. MacKinnon. <year>1994</year>. Electrostatic tuning of Mg<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> affinity in an inward-rectifier K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>371</volume>:<fpage>243</fpage>&#x02013;246.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7915826</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Magleby, K.L. <year>2003</